  "concern": "2026-09-14 user review of the product command bar: the selection read as secondary to the search field."
 },
 "changeSummary": [
  "Command bar is context-first: the committed record moves ahead of the finder, gains a brand edge, its zero-padded number in the brand ramp and its title at body size; Clear is demoted to quiet subtle text after a hairline rule.",
  "One finder, two presentations: with a record committed and a destination other than Overview, the search field and Show selection collapse into a single labelled Switch work control that reopens the same finder in one activation with query, scope and list position retained. No second picker and no extra selection confirmation were added.",
  "Now leads with an object header: zero-padded number plus name at 24px/32px (20px at <=719px) with kind, slug, path, stage badge, example labelling and the record-scoped Review design action attached to it. The breadcrumb keeps the number only, removing the title triplication.",
  "Prototype explanation is visibly outside the product: hatched band, a PROTOTYPE - NOT PART OF DUDE flag and a labelled edge. No required simulation label was hidden.",
  "Bar caption steps back from \"Working on\" to \"Browsing\" while a request with a different scope is open, so the dominant context cannot read as that request's scope."
 ],
 "defectsFoundAndFixed": [
  "rev-2 at 360px CSS width with a long title scrolled the page horizontally to 511px: the command-bar identity span and the breadcrumb that repeated the full title both escaped the viewport. Both are corrected; measured page scrollWidth is now 345px at 360px for 062 and for the longest recorded title (021), with zero elements past the viewport edge."
 ],
